protobuf provides the lite runtime in core. Request full-runtime explicitly
when linking protobuf::libprotobuf or using full generated messages, reflection,
descriptors, or text/JSON conversion. Existing applications that require these
APIs must update their manifest when adopting this port revision:

    {
      "name": "protobuf",
      "features": ["full-runtime"]
    }

Full runtime CMake usage:

    find_package(protobuf CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE protobuf::libprotobuf)

Lite runtime CMake usage:

    find_package(protobuf CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE protobuf::libprotobuf-lite)

Lite consumers must generate compatible messages, for example by adding
option optimize_for = LITE_RUNTIME; to their .proto files. Small messages do
not automatically use lite. Imported schemas and other dependencies must also
be compatible with the chosen runtime.

The host protoc compiler is installed automatically. Building compiler plugins
that link protobuf::libprotoc requires the libprotoc feature; this also enables
full-runtime. The zlib feature likewise enables full-runtime for gzip APIs.

Host and target requests for the same triplet share their features, so equal
host/target triplets still install full. A lite-only target requires distinct
triplets and no full-runtime request elsewhere in the target dependency graph.
An additional full-runtime request preserves protobuf::libprotobuf-lite.

Use the host protoc from this installation when generating C++ messages; the
generated code and runtime versions must match. CONFIG discovery supports both
protobuf and Protobuf spellings. Explicit protobuf_MODULE_COMPATIBLE requires
full-runtime.
